.git
# Note the `**/` on each of these. Docker anchors a pattern at the context root
# unless it starts with `**/`, so a bare `__pycache__/` or `.venv/` matches only a
# root-level one — and this repo has neither at the root (they live under
# app/server-python/). Without the prefix all three lines silently matched nothing:
# the 67MB venv was shipped to the daemon on every build, and src/__pycache__ +
# src/timeline/__pycache__ were copied into the image, carrying stale bytecode for
# modules that no longer exist. Verified by building a probe image that COPYs the
# whole context and lists it.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
# Docs aren't needed in the server image.
README.md
# The web client's source IS in the build context (the web-build stage needs it),
# but its install/build artifacts must not be — they'd bloat the context and the
# image rebuilds them from the lockfile anyway.
app/client-web/node_modules/
app/client-web/dist/
# Generated by the web-build stage inside the image; never ship a local copy.
app/server-python/src/static/
